  "adventure": {
    "origin_id": "9caf75b2-053d-4249-b353-577308cd3abd",
    "title": "Professor Quark's Quantum Quest",
    "teaser": "Survive broken physics, solve cosmic riddles, and reassemble your professor before reality implodes!",
    "cover_appearance": "floating university lecture hall, glowing quantum equations, swirling purple singularity, wacky sci-",
    "version": "3.0.0",
    "creator": "Jean Schmitz",
    "copyright": "Copyright (c) 2026 by Jean Schmitz",
    "license": "CC BY-NC 4.0",
    "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/",
    "language": "English",
    "original_prompt": "## One-Line Premise\nNavigate a crumbling, physics-defying university to help an eccentric, disembodied professor piece together the scattered fragments of the Grand Unified Theory before the universe reboots itself.\n\n## Plot Summary\nProfessor Quentin Quark, a brilliant but chronically disorganized astrophysicist, has accidentally triggered a localized \"Big Bounce\" within his own university. His consciousness is now scattered across various lecture halls, each transformed into a physical manifestation of a core cosmological concept. The player, an eager but bewildered first-year student trapped in the anomaly, must explore these bizarre rooms. In each space, a holographic, quirky projection of Professor Quark (representing a specific subfield like Quantum Mechanics or Relativity) explains the local physical laws and presents a thematic puzzle. To progress, the player must absorb the lesson, solve the environmental quiz, and collect a \"Paradigm Badge.\" Gathering all the badges is the only way to reassemble Quark's mind, complete the Grand Unified Theory equation, and stabilize the localized space-time continuum before the university collapses into a singularity.\n\n## Core Pillars\nGenre: Sci-Fi / Educational Comedy\nTone: Wacky, intellectual, slightly urgent (think \"Hitchhiker's Guide\" meets a physics textbook).\nPlayer Role: A desperate first-year physics student trying to survive finals week (and a literal universal collapse).\nMain Conflict: The breakdown of local physics vs. the player's ability to learn and apply complex concepts to fix it.\nAntagonistic Force: Entropy itself, manifesting as chaotic physics anomalies (e.g., reversed gravity, unpredictable time dilation).\nDistinctive World Rules: \n- Each room operates under different physical laws (e.g., in the Quantum Room, items change state when not observed).\n- The \"Quark-o-Meter\" tracks understanding; failing quizzes increases local entropy.\n- Badges alter the player's interaction with the environment (e.g., the \"Gravity Badge\" allows walking on walls).\nKey Locations: The Schrodinger Cafeteria, The Relativistic Library (where the clocks move at different speeds), The Dark Matter Boiler Room.\nFactions: The Standard Model Particles (helpful, orderly NPCs) vs. The Exotic Matter Anomalies (chaotic, disruptive entities).\nSignature NPC Ideas: \n- Hologram Quark (Relativity Mode): Speaks incredibly fast but moves very slowly.\n- Madam Entropy: The snarky head librarian who loves the chaos.\n- The Higgs Boson: A very shy janitor who gives mass to objects but is hard to find.\nMain Quest Seeds: Collect the 7 Paradigm Badges by passing Quark's quizzes.\nSide Quest Seeds: Help a lost electron find its orbital; resolve a time paradox in the library.\nWin Condition: Collect all badges, reconstruct Quark, and receive the \"Universal Constant Award\" to stabilize the anomaly.\nLose Condition: Local entropy reaches 100%, collapsing the university into a supermassive black hole.\n\n## Why It Works:\n- Novelty: Transforms abstract physics concepts into tangible, explorable, and humorous environments.\n- Educational Value: Forces players to understand the concepts to solve the puzzles, providing a gamified learning experience.\n- Emotional Arc: Moves from confusion and chaos to understanding and mastery of the universe's rules.\n- Systemic Potential: The badge system allows for metroidvania-style progression, where early badges solve later puzzles.",
    "image_url": "assets/cover_3531daed_a1a8a8e8-0520-414b-83d7-69432f301c65_cover_d3641e6b.jpg",
    "rule_enforcement_mode": "chat",
